From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system: the boot menu waits 5 seconds by default, one of four
 choices

Since 1.0 scripts/mkimage writes the boot menus with a wait of 5 seconds
(10 before), as the BIOS menu of LibreELEC waits. System > Boot menu
offers 10, 5, 3 and 1 seconds, and its help says that 5 is the default
and that an update keeps the choice: the installer for Windows now
carries it across an update, as an update in place always did.

Nothing else changes: the value is read from the menus each time the
list is shown (internal-disks wait), a wait set by hand is shown among
the ones offered, and choosing one writes it into both menus.
---
 resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po | 2 +-
 resources/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po | 4 ++--
 resources/language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po | 4 ++--
 resources/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po | 4 ++--
 resources/lib/modules/system.py                       | 6 +++---
 5 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

